  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows negative sentiment (e.g., -0.25 or 0.00 with recent declines) to account for bearish momentum.",
    "Reduce forecast volatility in early periods (e.g., first 5-7 days) when price is trending downward, as models tend to overreact.",
    "Apply mean reversion correction: if forecast is > 10% above recent 5-day average, reduce by 5-10% to avoid over-optimism.",
    "When sentiment shifts from neutral to positive (e.g., 0.50), slightly increase forecast but cap at 5% above prior peak to avoid overshoot.",
    "For long-term (30-day) forecasts, reduce the final 5-7 days if true outcome shows downward drift after a spike — model tends to overestimate continuation.",
    "If true outcome is consistently below forecast for 3 consecutive days, apply a 3-5% downward bias to next forecast to correct for persistent underperformance."
  ]
}
